chuckcar wrote:
>
> You can't gain experience quickly enough in fighting, besides, you need,
> what is it 60 (?) casts to go from unskilled to basic and another 30 to
> go up to the next. Now with a 1st level spell that's a total 450 spell
> points with none wasted - better to wait until you're over 50 spell
> points at least.

Manna recharges on its own.  As such it should be spent regularly.

> Besides, what will you do when you run out of spell points?

Be in greater danger.  Check.  So you want to run with a balance
of spell points enough to be able to cast a spell or two when in
trouble.  On the other hand going around with your manna fully
charged and at max is also a waste of resources.  Keep using
spells as long as you have plenty of food left.

With hit points you want to retreat when you get down towards
half max and heal.  With manna you actually want to use it
often enough that you deliberately drain it down towards half
max.  Keep the rest in reserve but also have the recharge
function have something to do.  In early game wizards spell
casting is limited by food availability not by manna recharge.

Later in the game spells no longer cost wizards food and they
get double recharge.  It starts being worth blasting away
almost constantly in what will seem a vien attempt to get down
to half max.  Early on half max is just another target to be
reached when the food's available.



